If a struct is used in a struct TS generates wrong code.
Example:

struct A {
  testBool: bool;
}

struct B {
  teststruct: A;
}

Furthermore:
- null value for type bool was wrong ("false" instead of "0")
- fixed reserved word argument -> arguments
- field accessor function must be unescaped

These changes add a feature to recurse through class object references to print the primitive fields that the object is composed of. For example, if we encounter an instance of `Shape` as a local variable, it will recurse through fields of the type `Shape`.

```java
public class Shape {
    String name;
    int sides;
}
```
In this case, `name` and `sides` will also be printed as attributes.

