Currently the initialization of accelerators does not work correctly, it segfaults in `CompilerUtils.cpp`:
```
(lldb) bt
* thread #1, queue = 'com.apple.main-thread', stop reason = EXC_BAD_ACCESS (code=1, address=0x0)
  * frame #0: 0x0000000100038360 onnx-mlir`std::__1::vector<mlir::Accelerator*, std::__1::allocator<mlir::Accelerator*> >::begin(this=0x0000000000000000) at vector:1517:30
    frame #1: 0x00000001000380b9 onnx-mlir`compileModule(module=0x00007ff7bfefec70, context=0x00007ff7bfefee68, outputBaseName="model", emissionTarget=EmitONNXIR) at CompilerUtils.cpp:1060:21
    frame #2: 0x0000000100004a8a onnx-mlir`main(argc=4, argv=0x00007ff7bfeff4f0) at onnx-mlir.cpp:80:10
    frame #3: 0x000000010a2cd4fe dyld`start + 462
```

The segfault happens because in the following code: 
```
  if (acceleratorTarget.compare("") != 0) {
    std::vector<Accelerator *> *accTargets  = Accelerator::getAcceleratorList();
    for (auto accel : *accTargets) {
```

The pointer `accTargets` is NULL.  That pointer is not initialized because the `Accelerator` constructor has not had a chance to run yet:

```
std::vector<Accelerator *> *Accelerator::acceleratorTargets;

Accelerator::Accelerator() {
  if (acceleratorTargets == NULL)
    acceleratorTargets = new std::vector<Accelerator *>();
}
```

This PR contains a fix for the segfault. It reworks the way Accelerators can be constructed. At high level I have introduced a factory method to create accelerators (see `Accelerator::create()`). This method also initializes the accelerator and adds it to a static list of available accelerators. The create accelerators we just invoke the factory method, which will create the correct type of accelerator based on `accelKind`: 

```
// Initialize accelerators if required.
  if (!maccel.empty()) {
    for (accel::Accelerator::Kind accelKind : maccel)
      accel::Accelerator::create(
          accelKind, module, context, pm, emissionTarget);
  }
```

I think this simplifies the Accelerator code because it preempts the need to track whether an accelerator is "active" and takes care of initializing the accelerators in the `create` factory method. 

